## 2.4 GHz radio
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-titulo = 2.4 GHz radio
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-desc = The transmitter for the 2.4 GHz band: if you turn it off, every network on that band goes off, including the guest network.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ayuda = The channel and width decide how much your WiFi and your neighbours' overlap. On automatic, the router picks a clear channel by itself. If WiFi is poor in a specific spot, try another channel. When a change is applied, every device on this band disconnects for a few seconds.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-encendida = Radio on
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-encendida-desc = Only turn it off if you don't use this band: devices connected over it lose WiFi.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-encendida-recomendado = Recommended if any device uses this band, as in almost every home. Pros: with both bands on, each device uses whichever suits it best. Cons: none significant for most people; turning it off only makes sense if nothing uses it.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal = Channel
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-desc = The specific frequency the WiFi uses within the band.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-automatico = Automatic
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-automatico-desc = The router picks the channel with the least interference by itself; you do not choose which one.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-recomendado = Recommended if your WiFi works well or you don't know which channels your neighbours use. Pros: the router looks for a clear channel by itself. Cons: it does not always get it right; if you notice dropouts in one area, a fixed channel may work better.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_1 = Channel 1
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_1-desc = One of the three channels that do not overlap (1, 6 and 11): good if it is the one your neighbours use least, but if it gets crowded, you will have to change it yourself.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_6 = Channel 6
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_6-desc = One of the three channels that do not overlap (1, 6 and 11): good if it is the one your neighbours use least, but if it gets crowded, you will have to change it yourself.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_11 = Channel 11
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-canal-canal_11-desc = One of the three channels that do not overlap (1, 6 and 11): good if it is the one your neighbours use least, but if it gets crowded, you will have to change it yourself.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho = Channel width
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-desc = How much room the WiFi takes up: wider gives more speed, but clashes more with the networks around.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-mhz_20 = 20 MHz
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-mhz_20-desc = The narrowest: lower top speed, but a steadier connection where there are many networks.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-mhz_40 = Up to 40 MHz
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-mhz_40-desc = Twice as wide: more speed if there are no networks nearby; if there are, it overlaps them and usually does worse.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24-ancho-recomendado = Recommended if there are other WiFi networks nearby, as is usual in flats and towns. Pros: your WiFi overlaps less with your neighbours' and the connection is steadier. Cons: the top speed on this band is lower than at 40 MHz.

## 2.4 GHz radio: more options
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-titulo = 2.4 GHz radio: more options
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-desc = Transmit power and compatibility with old devices.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-ayuda = The factory values are right almost every time. Lowering the power reduces range; dropping compatibility with old devices leaves those that only know those modes without WiFi.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia = Transmit power
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-desc = How strongly the radio transmits: more power, more range.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-automatica = Automatic
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-automatica-desc = The router sets the power by itself; you do not control how far it reaches.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-maxima = Maximum
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-maxima-desc = Full power: the longest possible range, although the WiFi also reaches further into your neighbours' homes.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-media = Medium
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-media-desc = Half: useful in a small home; in distant rooms the signal may arrive weak.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-baja = Low
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-baja-desc = 20% of the power: much less range; only if your devices are close to the router.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-potencia-recomendado = Recommended if you have no specific reason to change it. Pros: the router decides the power on its own, so you do not have to think about range. Cons: none significant for most people; if you want the WiFi to reach less far, you will have to pick a lower one.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo = Compatibility
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-desc = Which WiFi generations this radio accepts.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-bgn = All devices
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-bgn-desc = Supports 802.11b, g and n: no device is left out, not even those over twenty years old.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-gn = Without very old devices
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-gn-desc = Only 802.11g and n: devices that only know 802.11b (over twenty years old) cannot connect.
ajuste-wifi-radio_24_avanzado-modo-recomendado = Recommended if you or your visitors have very old devices, or you don't know. Pros: any device can connect, however old. Cons: while a very old one is connected, the WiFi may be somewhat slower for the rest.

## 5 GHz radio
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-titulo = 5 GHz radio
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-desc = The transmitter for the 5 GHz band: if you turn it off, every network on that band goes off.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ayuda = The channel and width decide the speed and how much your WiFi and your neighbours' overlap. On automatic, the router picks the channel by itself. When a change is applied, every device on this band disconnects for a few seconds; on the high channels they may take an extra minute to come back.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-encendida = Radio on
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-encendida-desc = Only turn it off if you don't use this band: devices connected over it lose WiFi.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-encendida-recomendado = Recommended if any device uses this band, as in almost every home. Pros: with both bands on, each device uses whichever suits it best. Cons: none significant for most people; turning it off only makes sense if nothing uses it.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal = Channel
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-desc = The specific frequency the WiFi uses within the band.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-automatico = Automatic
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-automatico-desc = The router picks the channel with the least interference by itself; you do not choose which one.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-recomendado = Recommended if your WiFi works well or you don't know which channels your neighbours use. Pros: the router looks for a clear channel by itself. Cons: it does not always get it right; if you notice dropouts in one area, a fixed channel may work better.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-canal_36 = Channel 36 (low band)
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-canal_36-desc = Low channels of the band: the WiFi starts right away, without waiting to check for nearby radars; in exchange, they allow less power than the high ones.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-canal_100 = Channel 100 (high band)
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-canal-canal_100-desc = High channels: they allow more power, but the router must listen for radar for a minute before transmitting and switch channel if it detects one.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho = Channel width
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-desc = How much room the WiFi takes up: wider gives more speed, but clashes more with the networks around.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_20 = 20 MHz
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_20-desc = The narrowest: lower top speed, but a steadier connection where there are many networks.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_40 = Up to 40 MHz
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_40-desc = A middle ground: more speed than at 20 MHz and fewer clashes with nearby networks than at 80 MHz.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_80 = Up to 80 MHz
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-mhz_80-desc = The widest: the highest speed this radio offers, although it clashes more with nearby 5 GHz networks.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5-ancho-recomendado = Recommended if you want the highest speed, as in almost every home. Pros: WiFi 5 devices go as fast as they can. Cons: if there are many 5 GHz networks nearby, it overlaps them more and a narrower width may be steadier.

## 5 GHz radio: more options
