ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-potencia-media-desc = Half: useful in a small home; in distant rooms the signal may arrive weak.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-potencia-baja = Low
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-potencia-baja-desc = 20% of the power: much less range; only if your devices are close to the router.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-potencia-recomendado = Recommended if you have no specific reason to change it. Pros: the router decides the power on its own, so you do not have to think about range. Cons: none significant for most people; if you want the WiFi to reach less far, you will have to pick a lower one.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo = Compatibility
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-desc = Which WiFi generations this radio accepts.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-anac = All devices
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-anac-desc = Accepts WiFi 5 (802.11ac) and the earlier ones on this band: the fastest option.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-an = Without WiFi 5
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-an-desc = Only 802.11a and 802.11n: modern devices go slower. Only for an old device that gives trouble.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-modo-recomendado = Recommended if you have any WiFi 5 device, like almost every current phone and laptop. Pros: those devices run at their top speed, and older ones can still connect. Cons: none significant for most people.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-beamforming = Directed signal (beamforming)
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-beamforming-desc = The router focuses the signal towards each device instead of spreading it evenly, which improves speed at a distance.
ajuste-wifi-radio_5_avanzado-beamforming-recomendado = Recommended if you want a better signal in rooms far from the router. Pros: it improves speed and coverage for devices that support it. Cons: none significant for most people; devices that do not support it work as before.
